<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-conquest-of-the-banda-islands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-conquest-of-the-banda-islands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch conquest of the Banda Islands</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1621</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch conquest of the Banda Islands was the seizure of these nutmeg-producing islands in 1621 by the Dutch East India Company under Jan Pieterszoon Coen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-east-india-company.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch East India Company</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch East India Company (VOC) was a chartered trading company founded in 1602, with powers to wage war, make treaties and govern territory in Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Empire was the overseas colonial and commercial empire of the Netherlands, built mainly from the seventeenth century by the Dutch East India Company and the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-golden-age"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-golden-age.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Golden Age</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Golden Age was the period, roughly the seventeenth century, when the Dutch Republic was among the richest and most powerful states in Europe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-reformed-church"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-reformed-church.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Reformed Church</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Reformed Church was the main Calvinist church of the Netherlands and the established church of the Dutch Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-republic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Republic</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Republic was the federal state of the United Provinces of the Netherlands that emerged from the revolt against Spain in the late sixteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · War · c. 1566–1648</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Revolt was the uprising of the Netherlands against Spanish Habsburg rule that began in the 1560s and led to the independence of the Dutch Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-water-line"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-water-line.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Water Line</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Water Line was a defensive line of fortified towns and low land that could be deliberately flooded, protecting the heartland of Holland on its eastern side.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/